// Generated GridLAB-D model from Pandapower
//
// ref_lv_bus_1 is the MV substation busbar (12.7 kV L-N -> ~22 kV L-L on ABCN,
// matching TRANSFORMER_MV_KV). Its LV network hangs off three distribution
// transformers (pcc_1..pcc_3) rather than lines, which is what makes each group
// a microgrid zone: the loader partitions on the line-only graph, so everything
// behind a transformer is one zone, and that transformer is the PCC tripped to
// island it. Zone codes come from the transformer names (1..3) — keep them below
// IOT_NUM_ZONES (default 10) or the parent bridge hashes them to an arbitrary
// zone_<n> stream instead of routing them (verified live: a code of 10 lands in
// zone_1, 11 in zone_8).
//
// The grid has four physical feeders; the fourth (ref_lv_bus_78/79/80, a short
// DER-less stub) is served from zone 3 over Line_54 instead of taking its own
// PCC, so the model has three zones.
module powerflow;
module generators;

